### star-idea-storm/SKILL.md
--- 1
Per kept direction, per `references/scan_policy.md` (Chinese dialogue: `references/scan_policy_zh.md`): build 2–3 queries, run them across the Semantic Scholar / arXiv / DBLP search endpoints plus web search, and collect 8–15 papers (title / venue / year / citations / one-clause relevance / record URL). Write that direction's §3 block as soon as its scan finishes: the scan table, a note on how crowded the area is (publication rate and trajectory, venues, named groups if evident, survey existence), the 3 closest works with what each one's abstract does **not** claim, and the apparent gap. Default depth is title + abstract; deepen — intro and related-work first paragraph of that direction's top-3 — only when the user names a direction or a gap claim decides between finalists, and record it in the block's `depth:` line. Scanning may fan out to read-only `subagent` subagents (`subagent_type: Explore`, `model: sonnet`), run in parallel, one direction each, each returning the collector format in `references/scan_policy.md` — the briefing, and each collector's share of the rate budget, are built by the main agent, never by the collector; the main agent writes the file and owns every judgment line. Surprises — crowded where empty was expected, a same-question preprint from the last 6 months — are reported the moment they are found, not at stage end. A failed search is reported as failed, never padded.
+++ 1
Per kept direction, per `references/scan_policy.md` (Chinese dialogue: `references/scan_policy_zh.md`): build 2–3 queries, run them across the Semantic Scholar / arXiv / DBLP search endpoints plus web search, and collect 8–15 papers (title / venue / year / citations / one-clause relevance / record URL). Write that direction's §3 block as soon as its scan finishes: the scan table, a note on how crowded the area is (publication rate and trajectory, venues, named groups if evident, survey existence), the 3 closest works with what each one's abstract does **not** claim, and the apparent gap. Default depth is title + abstract; deepen — intro and related-work first paragraph of that direction's top-3 — only when the user names a direction or a gap claim decides between finalists, and record it in the block's `depth:` line. Scanning may fan out to read-only `subagent` calls, run in parallel, one direction each, each returning the collector format in `references/scan_policy.md` — the briefing, and each collector's share of the rate budget, are built by the main agent, never by the collector; the main agent writes the file and owns every judgment line. Surprises — crowded where empty was expected, a same-question preprint from the last 6 months — are reported the moment they are found, not at stage end. A failed search is reported as failed, never padded.
### star-idea-storm/SKILL_zh.md
--- 1
对每个入围方向，按 `references/scan_policy.md`（中文对话读 `references/scan_policy_zh.md`）：起 2–3 个查询词，跑 Semantic Scholar / arXiv / DBLP 搜索端点加网页搜索，收 8–15 篇（标题 / venue / 年份 / 引用数 / 一小句相关性 / 记录 URL）。某方向扫完就立即写它的 §3 块：扫描表、竞争激烈程度说明（发文速率与走势、venue 分布、看得出的团队、有无综述）、3 篇最接近的工作及各自摘要**没有**声称的东西、表面缺口。默认深度为标题 + 摘要；只有用户指明某方向、或某条缺口判断直接决定两个入选方向的去留时才加深——读该方向 top-3 的 intro 与 related work 首段——并记录在该块的 `depth:` 行。扫描可派出只读收集器 `subagent` 子代理（`subagent_type: Explore`、`model: sonnet`），并行派发、每个负责一个方向、各自按 `references/scan_policy_zh.md` 的收集器返回格式返回——交办说明、以及按份数分给各收集器的速率配额，都由主 agent 构建，收集器绝不自己攒；主 agent 写文件，并亲自下所有判断行。意外——预期冷清处很拥挤、近 6 个月出现同问题 preprint——一发现就立刻说，不等阶段结束。搜索失败如实报告失败，绝不填充。
