### star-plan-executor/SKILL.md
--- 1
**The report is not the end of the turn.** With its text out, start `star-code-reviewer` on this leaf in the same reply — the `Skill` tool, `star-code-reviewer` as the skill and the leaf as its argument, the way Step 5 dispatches an `subagent` — to audit the implementation against the conventions and the sub-plan. It is one of the eight skills the agent may start and its target is settled, so it runs rather than prints: a command printed to the agent itself is a handoff to nobody (conventions §10.6). This is the run's last action in either ending — after a completed run, before revising or moving on; and before the user runs a command handed back at the STOP line.
+++ 1
**The report is not the end of the turn.** With its text out, start `star-code-reviewer` on this leaf in the same reply — the way this host starts a skill, the leaf as its argument, as Step 5 dispatches its subagent — to audit the implementation against the conventions and the sub-plan. It is one of the eight skills the agent may start and its target is settled, so it runs rather than prints: `star-code-reviewer <leaf>` printed to the agent itself is a handoff to nobody (conventions §10.6). This is the run's last action in either ending — after a completed run, before revising or moving on; and before the user runs a command handed back at the STOP line.
### star-plan-executor/SKILL.md
--- 1
- Involve (conventions §7.7). Always asked here: the exit_plan_mode confirmation point (Step 4, including its commit, execution-branch, and worktree questions), the STOP line (Step 5), the merge confirmation point and a branch's or worktree's discard, removal, or deletion (Step 7 — conventions §11), amendment sync (Step 6 — it writes plan §2–§5), the scratch offer, and what becomes of a blocked step's edits (each stops for confirmation before a deletion — `references/agent_dispatch_spec.md`). One of them moves at `low`: the Step 4 confirmation point is taken unasked. Plan mode is not entered (Step 3) and `exit_plan_mode` is not called, since Claude Code's plan dialog waits for a keypress that no hook can supply; the material is still presented in full in the reply, the questions riding that confirmation point take their recommended answers, and the decisions record logs the approval as taken unasked. Set to `low`: Step 0's which-leaf choice (take the first ready leaf in dependency order; a no-argument or ambiguous invocation still asks, conventions §5.2), Step 1's readiness fallback and its sizing check (take the recommendation: route back to the decomposer and stop), and Step 9's skip offer where an exploratory leaf's command is cheap (take the recommendation: start the review). Starting the review is not a question at any level — Step 9 states why, and neither is Step 4's hand-over of Step 5 to the EXEC tier: it changes which model runs the loop, not what the loop does. At `high`, confirm each step's dispatch (Step 5) before it goes to a subagent. Record the effective level and its source once in `EXEC_LOG.md`.
+++ 1
- Involve (conventions §7.7). Always asked here: the exit_plan_mode confirmation point (Step 4, including its commit, execution-branch, and worktree questions), the STOP line (Step 5), the merge confirmation point and a branch's or worktree's discard, removal, or deletion (Step 7 — conventions §11), amendment sync (Step 6 — it writes plan §2–§5), the scratch offer, and what becomes of a blocked step's edits (each stops for confirmation before a deletion — `references/agent_dispatch_spec.md`). One of them moves at `low`: the Step 4 confirmation point is taken unasked — plan mode is not entered (Step 3), the material is still presented in full in the reply, the questions riding that confirmation point take their recommended answers, and the decisions record logs the approval as taken unasked. Set to `low`: Step 0's which-leaf choice (take the first ready leaf in dependency order; a no-argument or ambiguous invocation still asks, conventions §5.2), Step 1's readiness fallback and its sizing check (take the recommendation: route back to the decomposer and stop), and Step 9's skip offer where an exploratory leaf's command is cheap (take the recommendation: start the review). Starting the review is not a question at any level — Step 9 states why, and neither is Step 4's hand-over of Step 5 to the EXEC tier: it changes which model runs the loop, not what the loop does. At `high`, confirm each step's dispatch (Step 5) before it goes to a subagent. Record the effective level and its source once in `EXEC_LOG.md`.
### star-plan-executor/SKILL_zh.md
--- 1
1. `EnterPlanMode`——`low` 档除外：那一档 Step 4 不问就放行，而 Claude Code 的 plan 审批对话框只等人按键、任何 hook 都替不了，所以 EXEC_PLAN 在 plan 模式之外起草，其余不变。
+++ 1
1. 请用户打开 plan 模式。DSH 没有进入它的工具——plan 模式是由人来选的会话状态，而 `exit_plan_mode` 在模式之外调用会失败。用户不开、或当前界面根本没有 plan 模式时，Step 4 走它的纯文本退路，其余一切照旧。`low` 档不请用户开：那一档 Step 4 不问就放行，EXEC_PLAN 在 plan 模式之外起草，其余不变。
### star-plan-executor/SKILL_zh.md
--- 1
**发起确认之前先跑设计检查。** 把 `references/design_check.md` 交出去做一次"不知情"的复核：一个只读 `subagent` 子代理（`subagent_type: Explore`），交办材料正好三个文件——刚写出的 EXEC_PLAN、叶子子计划、根计划只读它的 §4——检查表认作证据的唯一一节根计划内容（计划 frontmatter 写着 `language: zh` 时改点名检查表的 `_zh` 那份；受托者绝不自己选）——范围逐字写明："只看这三个文件，根计划只看 §4。不排序、不决定、不运行任何东西。"它按条返回 `item`、`verdict: pass | fail | unclear`、`evidence`、`fix`。主 agent 对每一条打算上报的 `fail` 都回去打开被引用的那一行——判"缺失"的 `fail` 引不出行，那就重读该条目所属的整节——然后把至多五条发现摆在确认调用**上方**，一条一行;确认不了的 `fail` 丢掉。检查只报告；做决定的是这个确认点，这里不叫停任何 run。没有受托者可用时，检查表由主 agent 自己跑（规约 §6.1）。
